{"availability":"available","full":"aghasalim/eu-ai-act-rag","name":"eu-ai-act-rag","description":"Grounded question answering over the EU AI Act, with retrieval, faithfulness and hallucination measured on 45 hand-written questions.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":4,"forks":0,"created":"2026-08-13T12:06:05Z","updated":"2026-10-10T22:07:05Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":null,"topics":["eu-ai-act","hybrid-search","information-retrieval","llm-evaluation","machine-learning","nlp","rag","ragas","retrieval-augmented-generation","streamlit"],"demo":"https://eu-ai-act-rag-eval.streamlit.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:36.270Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:36.270Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:36.270Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-12T08:00:36.270Z","stars":4,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["▶ Live demo · every answer shows the passages it came from.","I built a question-answering system over Regulation (EU) 2024/1689 (the EU AI Act), as amended by Regulation (EU) 2026/1744 (the \"Digital Omnibus on AI\"). The corpus is versioned by the date of the text. 2026-07-27 is the consolidated text and the default. 2024-07-12 is the original Official Journal text, which I kept so the two can be compared.","Most RAG projects, mine included, stop at \"look, it answers questions\" and never check whether the answer is in the documents retrieved. I wanted to measure that properly. So I wrote 45 questions by hand, scored the system against them and wrote down the failures. Retrieval is decent. 90.9% of questions get at least one correct provision. It's bad at questions that need two articles at once, though, and only 41.7% of those get everything they need. I'd rather show you that number than hide it. Every figure here is recomputed from the per-question records by independent implementations in…"],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aghasalim/eu-ai-act-rag/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4949684f3b3c5e388f83f014ab739b62fb500e5ce15634cf5569b9cf3e957153","extractedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:36.358Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:36.358Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"▶ Live demo · every answer shows the passages it came from.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aghasalim/eu-ai-act-rag/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"The labels, with a note on each mistake, are in eval/humanlabels.jsonl, and I made all of them myself. make agreement compares them with the stored outputs, so it needs no API key.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aghasalim/eu-ai-act-rag/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"api_key","status":"required","text":"It needs no API key and makes no LLM calls, so it's free. make eval-versions adds the runs on the amended text and the amended questions. make eval-paragraph compares article and paragraph chunks, and make eval-extended runs the 122-question set.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aghasalim/eu-ai-act-rag/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"4949684f3b3c5e388f83f014ab739b62fb500e5ce15634cf5569b9cf3e957153","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aghasalim/eu-ai-act-rag/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:36.358Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-10T22:07:05Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/aghasalim/eu-ai-act-rag/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-12T08:00:36.359Z","hash":"4949684f3b3c5e388f83f014ab739b62fb500e5ce15634cf5569b9cf3e957153","originalBytes":19552,"storedBytes":19552,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["article","questions","answer","text","paragraph","make","notes","them","amended","every","recall","retrieval","they","full","only","citation","two","eval","one","original","chunks","articles","euactrag","same","gold","judge","methods.md","numbers","against","answers","corpus","each","questions.","there","were","correct","hybrid"